The Jac walker "EnsureUniqueItem" is created to start at the Root node. It checks for exactly one outgoing node of archetype 'UniqueItem'. If none exists, it creates one attached to the root. It then reports the attached UniqueItem node. The safe check-then-create pattern is used.

```jac
node UniqueItem {}

walker EnsureUniqueItem {
    can start with Root entry {
        unique_items = [-->][?:UniqueItem];
        if unique_items.count() == 0 {
            new_item = here ++> UniqueItem();
            report new_item;
        } else {
            # If there are multiple, just report the first one
            report unique_items[0];
        }
    }
}
```

The Jac walker named SquaresStats is created to take a list of numbers as input. It computes the squares of the numbers and reports this list as the first report. Then it calculates the sum and average of these squares and reports them as a dictionary in the second report.

```jac
walker SquaresStats {
    can start with any entry {
        squares = [];
        for num in entry {
            squares.append(num * num);
        }
        report squares;

        sum_squares = 0;
        for sq in squares {
            sum_squares += sq;
        }
        avg_squares = 0;
        if squares.length > 0 {
            avg_squares = sum_squares / squares.length;
        }
        report {"sum": sum_squares, "average": avg_squares};
    }
}
```

