The Jac walker named `UniqueItemEnsurer` is created. It starts at the root node and checks for outgoing nodes of archetype `UniqueItem`. If none are found, it creates one connected to the root. It then reports the single attached `UniqueItem` node. This uses the safe check-then-create pattern as requested.

```jac
node UniqueItem {}

walker UniqueItemEnsurer {
    can start with Root entry {
        # Find all UniqueItem nodes connected from root
        unique_items = [here -->][?:UniqueItem];
        # If none found, create one attached to root
        if unique_items.count() == 0 {
            created = here ++> UniqueItem();
            unique_items = [created];
        }
        # Report the single attached UniqueItem node
        report unique_items[0];
